Now updateHUD. Original:
```
function updateHUD(){ui.home...;ui.status...;if(powerEffect)...;ui.power.classList.toggle(...);}
```
Add glue status logic. Need check players lengths and pesi. We want to show human ability pill only for human Pessi, and AI Pessi status maybe. Let's write:

```
function updateHUD(){
 ui...;
 ...
 const hp=players.find(q=>q.pesi&&q.human), ap=players.find(q=>q.pesi&&!q.human);
 const p=hp||ap;
 if(p){
   ui.glueBtn.classList.toggle('hidden',!hp);
   const label = hp?'GLUE DRIBBLE':'PESSI AI · GLUE';
   if(glueMsgTime>0){ui.glueStatus.textContent=glueMsg;ui.glueStatus.classList.add('show','hot');}
   else if(p.glue>0){ui.glueStatus.textContent=`✦ ${label} · ${p.glue.toFixed(1)}s`;...}
   else if(p.glueCd>0){ui.glueStatus.textContent=`✦ ${label} READY IN ${Math.ceil(p.glueCd)}s`; show, not hot}
   else {ui.glueStatus.textContent=`✦ ${label} READY`; show, hot?} // hot when ready maybe subtle
 } else {hide btn & pill}
}
```
`glueMsgTime` decremented in update. If showStarSelect calls updateHUD before started, okay.

For AI, show cooldown/active status, which is informative. For classic hide.

Set `ui.glueBtn.classList.toggle('active-ability', !!p && p.glue>0)`. `ready` class when p.glueCd<=0 && !p.glue and human.

Also `ui.glueStatus.classList.toggle('show', !!p)` etc. Careful glueMsgTime>0 with no pesi? no.

Let's edit.

